Credits for the colour themes in this directory

Each .theme file carries its own header with its origin, authors, and
licence. This file collects those headers in one place.

tokyo-night.theme
  Origin: rhizome's default colours. The bar, prompt, message, border,
    and recording colours come from the Tokyo Night palette; the
    launcher and menu purples, the unfocused border, and the shadow
    base are rhizome's own.
  Authors: Tokyo Night palette by Enkia (tokyo-night-vscode-theme,
    https://github.com/tokyo-night/tokyo-night-vscode-theme), also
    carried by folke's tokyonight.nvim
    (https://github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim, Apache-2.0); rhizome's
    colours by Glenn Thompson.
  Licence: the palette is MIT, "Copyright (c) 2018-present Enkia"; the
    full MIT notice is in tokyo-night.theme. The file is part of
    rhizome, AGPL-3.0-or-later.

The themes below are converted from Emacs colour themes by
tools/theme-convert. Each keeps the licence of the Emacs theme it
derives from, GPL-3.0-or-later. rhizome is AGPL-3.0-or-later; section
13 of the GPLv3 and section 13 of the AGPLv3 permit combining the two.

